<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="64074" href="schedule/2018/spring/ECON/590/64074.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120181" href="schedule/2018/spring.xml">Spring 2018</term><subject id="ECON" href="schedule/2018/spring/ECON.xml">Economics</subject><course id="590" href="schedule/2018/spring/ECON/590.xml">Individual Study and Research</course></parents><sectionNumber>7  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Applied Microeconometrics</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course covers econometric methods for applications in the fields of applied microeconomics.  This course will discuss both treatment effects methods (difference-in-difference, instrumental variables, and regression discontinuity) and structural methods (discrete choice, games, production function estimation). The objective of the course is to prepare students to conduct empirical research in applied microeconomics with frontier methods.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionDeptRestriction>Restricted to students in the Economics department.</sectionDeptRestriction><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2018-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2018-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>219</roomNumber><buildingName>David Kinley Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Borgschulte" firstName="M">Borgschulte, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Marshall" firstName="G">Marshall, G</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>